    "title": "Gen Z Becomes Most Interstate-Mobile Generation for First Time: Report - Whatfinger News Quick Hits",
    "text": "A truck towing a moving trailer near Rio Vista, Calif., on Sept. 15, 2023. Josh Edelson/AFP via Getty Images\nGeneration Z, including those aged 18 to 29, for the first time has become the most interstate mobile generation, according to a March 25 analysis from StorageCafe. More than 2.2 million of America’s youngest adults moved to a different state in 2024, surpassing millennials, who had dominated this category for years.\nWe had a problem loading this article. Please enable javascript or use a different browser. If the issue persists, please visit our help center.\nRead Full Article: https://www.theepochtimes.com/us/gen-z-becomes-most-interstate-mobile-generation-for-first-time-report-6006972/?utm_source=partner&utm_campaign=whatfinger",
